<title>FRANCE: Groupe Paribas 1996 profit 4.35 bln Ffr.</title>
<headline>Groupe Paribas 1996 profit 4.35 bln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net attributable	     profit    4,350  vs   loss  3,998</p>
<p>    Total net			profit    5,602  vs   loss  2,549</p>
<p>    Net Banking revenue		     28,838  vs	  26,182</p>
<p>    Other revenues			     7,605  vs   loss    286</p>
<p>    Dividend (francs)			     13  vs		12</p>
<p>    Net before provisions and tax	 13,219  vs profit  4,583</p>
<p>    Provisions				   5,581  vs	   4,981</p>
<p>    Tax					    2,036  vs	   2,151</p>
<p>    Minority interests	   loss	1,252  vs   loss  1,449</p>
<p>    General expenses			  23,224  vs	  21,313</p>
<p>    Total revenue from operations	 36,443  vs	  25,896</p>
<p>Paribas net attributable income breakdown by business unit.</p>
<p>    Banque Paribas		    profit 1,661  vs   loss 3,720</p>
<p>    Paribas principal Investments profit 3,197  vs profit 2,173</p>
<p>    Cie Bancaire			  loss   583  vs profit   338</p>
<p>    Credit du Nord		    profit   190  vs profit     3</p>
<p>    Structure			     loss   115  vs   loss 2,792</p>
<p>NOTE: The company said Cie Bancaire retained exceptional provisions for 2.5 billion francs to eliminate real estate risks. The Groupe's banks retained provisions for future technology expenses related to the transition to the single European currency. The exceptional items, for which provisions were retained in 1995, have ceased to have a negative impact on the accounts.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
